IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 3), 2002 Revised Edition: every provision other than reg 3
-- (in sgta-i-rg3-class.l4): the definitions, registration, fees, duration, general conditions, savings and the eight Schedules.
-- Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-class-licences-regulations-2000/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG3.txt.
-- The regulations grant class licences to OPERATORS of telecommunication systems and services.  What the seven amending instruments
-- change is in sgta-i-rg3-amendments.l4.

§ `Rg 3 regulation 2: definitions`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:53 | 2. In these Regulations —
-- src:TA1999-RG3:54 | "class licence" means a licence granted by the Authority under section 5 of the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:55 | Act as set out in the First, Second, Third, Fourth, Fifth, Sixth and Seventh
-- src:TA1999-RG3:56 | Schedules;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:57 | “Facilities-Based Operator” or “FBO” means a person who is granted a specific
-- src:TA1999-RG3:58 | licence under section 5 of the Act to run any telecommunication system
-- src:TA1999-RG3:59 | for the purpose of offering to other persons all or any of the following:
-- src:TA1999-RG3:60 | (a) telecommunication switching capacity;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:61 | (b) telecommunication switching services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:62 | (c) telecommunication transmission capacity; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:63 | (d) telecommunication transmission services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:64 | "licensee" means a person who is deemed to have been granted a class licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:65 | "operator" means a person who runs any of the specified telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG3:66 | systems and services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:67 | “Services-Based Operator” or “SBO” means a person who leases from an FBO
-- src:TA1999-RG3:68 | any telecommunication system (including telecommunication network
-- src:TA1999-RG3:69 | elements such as transmission capacity, switching services, ducts and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:70 | fibre) to provide telecommunication services to third parties or to resell
-- src:TA1999-RG3:71 | the telecommunication services of FBOs;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:72 | "specified telecommunication systems and services" means telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG3:73 | systems and services specified in the class licences.
@ref Rg 3 reg 2 (src:TA1999-RG3:53-73)
GIVEN `it is a licence granted by the Authority under section 5 of the Act as set out in the First, Second, Third, Fourth, Fifth, Sixth or Seventh Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 2: this is a "class licence"` MEANS
    `it is a licence granted by the Authority under section 5 of the Act as set out in the First, Second, Third, Fourth, Fifth, Sixth or Seventh Schedule`

GIVEN `the person is granted a specific licence under section 5 of the Act to run a telecommunication system to offer others switching capacity, switching services, transmission capacity or transmission services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 2: the person is a "Facilities-Based Operator" or "FBO"` MEANS
    `the person is granted a specific licence under section 5 of the Act to run a telecommunication system to offer others switching capacity, switching services, transmission capacity or transmission services`

GIVEN `the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 2: the person is a "licensee"` MEANS
    `the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence`

GIVEN `the person runs any of the specified telecommunication systems and services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 2: the person is an "operator"` MEANS
    `the person runs any of the specified telecommunication systems and services`

GIVEN `the person leases from an FBO a telecommunication system to provide services to third parties or to resell the services of FBOs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 2: the person is a "Services-Based Operator" or "SBO"` MEANS
    `the person leases from an FBO a telecommunication system to provide services to third parties or to resell the services of FBOs`

GIVEN `the system or service is specified in the class licences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 2: this is a "specified telecommunication system and service"` MEANS
    `the system or service is specified in the class licences`

§ `Rg 3 regulations 4 to 8: registration, fees, duration, codes of practice, waiver`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:84 | 4. An operator shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG3:85 | (a) register with the Authority in such form; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:86 | (b) submit to the Authority upon registration such information in writing relating
-- src:TA1999-RG3:87 | to his particulars and the description and scope of telecommunication systems and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:88 | services run by him,
-- src:TA1999-RG3:89 | as the Authority may require.
@ref Rg 3 reg 4 (src:TA1999-RG3:84-89)
GIVEN `the operator registered with the Authority in the form it required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operator submitted in writing the particulars and the description and scope of the systems and services it runs, as the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 4: the operator has registered as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the operator registered with the Authority in the form it required` AND `the operator submitted in writing the particulars and the description and scope of the systems and services it runs, as the Authority required`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:92 | 5. An operator shall upon registration or renewal of registration, as the case may be, pay
-- src:TA1999-RG3:93 | the fee specified in the Eighth Schedule, if any, appropriate to the type of specified
-- src:TA1999-RG3:94 | telecommunication systems and services run by him.
@ref Rg 3 reg 5 (src:TA1999-RG3:92-94)
GIVEN `the operator paid the fee, if any, that the Eighth Schedule specifies for the type of systems and services it runs, on registration or renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 5: the operator has paid the registration fee` MEANS
    `the operator paid the fee, if any, that the Eighth Schedule specifies for the type of systems and services it runs, on registration or renewal`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:97 | 6. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), the registration of a class licence and any renewal
-- src:TA1999-RG3:98 | thereof shall continue in force for a period of 3 years from the date of registration or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:99 | renewal, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:100 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to the registration of the following class licences for
-- src:TA1999-RG3:101 | which there is no renewal of registration:
-- src:TA1999-RG3:102 | (a) class licence for store-and-retrieve value-added network services (as set out in
-- src:TA1999-RG3:103 | the First Schedule) where no leased circuits are used;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:104 | (b) class licence for the resale of public switched telecommunication services (as
-- src:TA1999-RG3:105 | set out in the Third Schedule);
-- src:TA1999-RG3:106 | (c) class licence for public chain payphone services (as set out in the Fourth
-- src:TA1999-RG3:107 | Schedule).
@ref Rg 3 reg 6 (src:TA1999-RG3:97-107)
GIVEN `years since the registration or renewal` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a class licence that has no renewal of registration (store-and-retrieve value-added network services with no leased circuits, resale of public switched telecommunication services, public chain payphone services)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 6: the registration is still in force` MEANS
    `it is a class licence that has no renewal of registration (store-and-retrieve value-added network services with no leased circuits, resale of public switched telecommunication services, public chain payphone services)` OR (`years since the registration or renewal` LESS THAN 3)

-- src:TA1999-RG3:110 | 7. The conditions set out in these Regulations are in addition to any code of practice or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:111 | standard of performance issued or approved under section 26 of the Act which applies to
-- src:TA1999-RG3:112 | the licensee.
@ref Rg 3 reg 7 (src:TA1999-RG3:110-112)
GIVEN `a code of practice or standard of performance under section 26 of the Act applies to the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 7: the licensee must meet the conditions of these Regulations in addition to the code of practice or standard of performance` MEANS
    `a code of practice or standard of performance under section 26 of the Act applies to the licensee`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:115 | 8. The Minister, or the Authority subject to any direction by the Minister, may —
-- src:TA1999-RG3:116 | (a) waive the application of all or any of the provisions of these Regulations or all
-- src:TA1999-RG3:117 | or any of the conditions of any class licence in respect of any person; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:118 | (b) waive any fee or part thereof payable under these Regulations.
@ref Rg 3 reg 8 (src:TA1999-RG3:115-118)
GIVEN `the Minister, or the Authority subject to any direction by the Minister, waives the provision or condition, or the fee, for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 8: the provision, condition or fee does not apply to the person` MEANS
    `the Minister, or the Authority subject to any direction by the Minister, waives the provision or condition, or the fee, for the person`

§ `Rg 3 regulations 9 to 15: general conditions and savings`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:124 | 9. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), it is a condition of every class licence that the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:125 | must not establish or provide any telecommunication link outside the licensee’s premises,
-- src:TA1999-RG3:126 | whether by wire, cable, radio, fibre optics or otherwise, for the purpose of connecting its
-- src:TA1999-RG3:127 | systems to any other telecommunication system or equipment without the prior approval
-- src:TA1999-RG3:128 | of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:129 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to any internal telecommunication link within the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:130 | licensee’s premises.
@ref Rg 3 reg 9 (src:TA1999-RG3:124-130)
GIVEN `the licensee establishes or provides a telecommunication link outside its premises to connect its systems to another telecommunication system or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the link is an internal telecommunication link within the licensee's premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 9: the licensee may establish or provide the link` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee establishes or provides a telecommunication link outside its premises to connect its systems to another telecommunication system or equipment`) OR `the link is an internal telecommunication link within the licensee's premises` OR `the Authority gave its prior approval`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:133 | 10. —(1) It is a condition of every class licence that a licensee who provides services to
-- src:TA1999-RG3:134 | the public must publish information about the services it provides, including details such
-- src:TA1999-RG3:135 | as, but not limited to, the description of each service available, the charges, quality of
-- src:TA1999-RG3:136 | service standards, customer support services and other service terms and conditions.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:137 | (2) The information referred to in paragraph (1) must be published in such manner as
-- src:TA1999-RG3:138 | the Authority may direct, or in the absence of the Authority’s direction, in the manner
-- src:TA1999-RG3:139 | that the licensee sees fit.
@ref Rg 3 reg 10 (src:TA1999-RG3:133-139)
GIVEN `the licensee provides services to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee published the description, charges, quality of service standards, customer support services and other terms of each service, in the manner the Authority directed or, absent a direction, as it sees fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 10: the licensee has published the information the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee provides services to the public`) OR `the licensee published the description, charges, quality of service standards, customer support services and other terms of each service, in the manner the Authority directed or, absent a direction, as it sees fit`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:142 | 11. It is a condition of every class licence that any licensee who intends to collect
-- src:TA1999-RG3:143 | money deposits or to use prepaid cards (other than credit cards) as a means of collecting
-- src:TA1999-RG3:144 | payment from its customers must take such measures as the Authority considers
-- src:TA1999-RG3:145 | necessary to ensure that it is able to refund any balance due to such customers in the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:146 | event of default in the provision of its services.
@ref Rg 3 reg 11 (src:TA1999-RG3:142-146)
GIVEN `the licensee intends to collect money deposits or use prepaid cards (other than credit cards)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee took the measures the Authority considers necessary to refund any balance due on default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 11: the licensee has met the financial requirement` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee intends to collect money deposits or use prepaid cards (other than credit cards)`) OR `the licensee took the measures the Authority considers necessary to refund any balance due on default`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:149 | 12. It is a condition of every class licence that the licensee must comply with such
-- src:TA1999-RG3:150 | advisory guidelines relating to fair practices and conduct as may be issued under section
-- src:TA1999-RG3:151 | 28 of the Act for telecommunication service providers.
@ref Rg 3 reg 12 (src:TA1999-RG3:149-151)
GIVEN `the licensee complies with the advisory guidelines on fair practices and conduct issued under section 28 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 12: the licensee has met the condition` MEANS
    `the licensee complies with the advisory guidelines on fair practices and conduct issued under section 28 of the Act`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:154 | 13. It is a condition of every class licence that the licensee must, if directed by the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:155 | Authority —
-- src:TA1999-RG3:156 | (a) appoint at its own expense a separate and independent auditor to audit its
-- src:TA1999-RG3:157 | activities to determine whether the licensee has complied with the conditions of
-- src:TA1999-RG3:158 | class licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:159 | (b) submit the audited accounts and other reports prepared by the auditor to the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:160 | Authority for its inspection.
@ref Rg 3 reg 13 (src:TA1999-RG3:154-160)
GIVEN `the Authority directed the licensee to appoint an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee appointed, at its own expense, a separate and independent auditor and submitted the audited accounts and other reports to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 13: the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority directed the licensee to appoint an auditor`) OR `the licensee appointed, at its own expense, a separate and independent auditor and submitted the audited accounts and other reports to the Authority`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:163 | 14. It is a condition of every class licence that the licensee notifies the Authority of any
-- src:TA1999-RG3:164 | change or inaccuracy in its particulars, the description and scope of telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG3:165 | systems and services run by it and any other information submitted to the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-RG3:166 | these Regulations or the conditions of licence.
@ref Rg 3 reg 14 (src:TA1999-RG3:163-166)
GIVEN `the licensee notified the Authority of any change or inaccuracy in its particulars, the description and scope of its systems and services and any other information submitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 14: the licensee has notified the Authority` MEANS
    `the licensee notified the Authority of any change or inaccuracy in its particulars, the description and scope of its systems and services and any other information submitted`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:171 | 15. —(1) Any class licence for store-and-retrieve value-added network services,
-- src:TA1999-RG3:172 | audiotex services, resale of public switched telecommunication services and public chain
-- src:TA1999-RG3:173 | payphone services granted under the revoked Telecommunication (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3:174 | Regulations (Rg 10, 1999 Ed.) shall be deemed to have been granted under, and subject
-- src:TA1999-RG3:175 | to, the corresponding provisions of these Regulations and any registration in respect
-- src:TA1999-RG3:176 | thereof shall expire or be renewable under these Regulations on the date on which it
-- src:TA1999-RG3:177 | would have expired or been renewable had these Regulations not been enacted.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:178 | (2) Any person who was granted a class licence for Bulletin Board Services under the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:179 | revoked Telecommunication (Class Licences) Regulations shall be deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RG3:180 | granted a class licence for store-and-retrieve value-added network services where no
-- src:TA1999-RG3:181 | leased circuits are used.
@ref Rg 3 reg 15 (src:TA1999-RG3:171-181)
GIVEN `the licence was granted under the revoked Telecommunication (Class Licences) Regulations (Rg 10, 1999 Ed.) for store-and-retrieve value-added network services, audiotex services, resale of public switched telecommunication services or public chain payphone services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was granted a class licence for Bulletin Board Services under the revoked Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 15: the licence is deemed to have been granted under these Regulations` MEANS
    `the licence was granted under the revoked Telecommunication (Class Licences) Regulations (Rg 10, 1999 Ed.) for store-and-retrieve value-added network services, audiotex services, resale of public switched telecommunication services or public chain payphone services`
    OR `the person was granted a class licence for Bulletin Board Services under the revoked Regulations`

§ `Rg 3 First to Fourth Schedules: the class licences`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:190 | 1. Store-and-retrieve value-added network services are any of the following services
-- src:TA1999-RG3:191 | provided by telecommunication systems, built over and above the telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG3:192 | systems operated by an FBO and accessed through public telecommunication systems or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:193 | leased circuits, which allow telecommunication traffic between a user and the value-
-- src:TA1999-RG3:194 | added network or between users:
-- src:TA1999-RG3:195 | (a) on-line information and database retrieval services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:196 | (b) on-line information and data processing services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:197 | (c) voice information services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:198 | (d) electronic broking services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:199 | (e) transaction services such as on-line shopping, on-line reservation service, etc.;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:200 | (f) remote computing services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:201 | (g) on-line games;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:202 | (h) mailbox services including e-mailbox, voice-mailbox, facsimile-mailbox and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:203 | multimedia mailbox;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:204 | (i) electronic data interchange services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:205 | (j) store-and-retrieve file transfer services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:206 | (k) electronic chatting services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:207 | (l) bulletin board services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:208 | (m) other multimedia services where the content or format of the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:209 | telecommunication traffic is changed or processed.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:211 | Conditions to be complied by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:212 | 2. A licensee must ensure that no store-and-forward telecommunication traffic is carried
-- src:TA1999-RG3:213 | through the value-added network.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:214 | 3. A licensee must not, except with the prior approval of the Authority, provide value-
-- src:TA1999-RG3:215 | added network services of another value-added network through a leased circuit
-- src:TA1999-RG3:216 | connecting its value-added network to the other value-added network.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:217 | 4. In the event that a licensee decides to terminate its value-added network services, it
-- src:TA1999-RG3:218 | must notify the Authority in writing of its intent.
@ref Rg 3 First Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:190-218)
GIVEN `service` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 First Schedule item 1: this is a store-and-retrieve value-added network service` MEANS
    elem service (LIST "on-line information and database retrieval services", "on-line information and data processing services", "voice information services", "electronic broking services"
                     , "transaction services such as on-line shopping, on-line reservation service", "remote computing services", "on-line games"
                     , "mailbox services including e-mailbox, voice-mailbox, facsimile-mailbox and multimedia mailbox", "electronic data interchange services"
                     , "store-and-retrieve file transfer services", "electronic chatting services", "bulletin board services"
                     , "other multimedia services where the content or format of the telecommunication traffic is changed or processed")

GIVEN `the licensee ensures no store-and-forward telecommunication traffic is carried through the value-added network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee provides value-added network services of another value-added network through a leased circuit connecting the two` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee notified the Authority in writing of its intent to terminate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 First Schedule items 2 to 4: the licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `the licensee ensures no store-and-forward telecommunication traffic is carried through the value-added network`
    AND ((NOT `the licensee provides value-added network services of another value-added network through a leased circuit connecting the two`) OR `the Authority gave its prior approval`)
    AND `the licensee notified the Authority in writing of its intent to terminate`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:226 | 1. Audiotex services are telecommunication systems and services which enable a caller,
-- src:TA1999-RG3:227 | by dialling a designated telephone number beginning with “1900”, to receive a recorded
-- src:TA1999-RG3:228 | announcement or to interact with a programme whereby he may communicate, by means
-- src:TA1999-RG3:229 | of a dual-tone multi-frequency telephone key pad, a touch-tone telephone or other similar
-- src:TA1999-RG3:230 | device, with a value-added network connected to the public switched telephone system
-- src:TA1999-RG3:231 | for the purposes of sending or receiving information.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:233 | Conditions to be complied by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:234 | 2. Access to the audiotex services by users must be through the public switched
-- src:TA1999-RG3:235 | network.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:236 | 3. A licensee must ensure that all announcements and programmes on the audiotex
-- src:TA1999-RG3:237 | services are pre-recorded and stored in the audiotex system and must not enable callers to
-- src:TA1999-RG3:238 | communicate directly in real-time with other callers.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:239 | 4. A licensee must comply with the following transmission standards:
-- src:TA1999-RG3:240 | (a) there must be no delay in starting the announcement or programme when a call
-- src:TA1999-RG3:241 | is connected;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:242 | (b) each audiotex service must be assigned a different telephone number;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:243 | (c) there must be no interruption during the announcement or programme;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:244 | (d) each call must be for a maximum period of 10 minutes with an option for the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:245 | caller to extend his call;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:246 | (e) where callers are required to enter a unique code to access the audiotex
-- src:TA1999-RG3:247 | services, such codes must be made available to the public either in lists published
-- src:TA1999-RG3:248 | by the licensee or through a telephone answering line available for enquiries 24
-- src:TA1999-RG3:249 | hours a day, the number for which must be published in all advertisements for the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:250 | audiotex services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:251 | 5. A licensee must ensure that the number of attempted calls at any time does not
-- src:TA1999-RG3:252 | significantly exceed the number of call-in lines for the audiotex services and, if the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:253 | Authority determines that additional lines are required to adequately handle calls for the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:254 | audiotex services and to prevent congestion to other users of the public switched
-- src:TA1999-RG3:255 | telephone system, the licensee must subscribe for such number of additional lines as the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:256 | Authority may direct.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:257 | 6. A licensee must not, except with the prior approval of the Authority, organise any
-- src:TA1999-RG3:258 | mass calling event which will generate a high influx of calls to its audiotex system.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:259 | 7. A licensee must ensure that its current call charging rate is published in all
-- src:TA1999-RG3:260 | advertisements for the audiotex services and is announced at the beginning of a pre-
-- src:TA1999-RG3:261 | recorded charge announcement played immediately after every call is connected.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:262 | 8. A licensee must provide a grace period during which callers are not charged, of —
-- src:TA1999-RG3:263 | (a) the first 6 seconds of a call where the charge announcement lasts less than 4
-- src:TA1999-RG3:264 | seconds; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:265 | (b) the first 12 seconds of a call where the charge announcement lasts between 4
-- src:TA1999-RG3:266 | seconds and 10 seconds.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:267 | 9. A licensee must not claim any propriety right to any telephone number assigned to it.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:268 | 10. If a licensee decides to terminate its audiotex services, it must notify the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG3:269 | in writing of its intent.
@ref Rg 3 Second Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:226-269)
GIVEN `the caller dials a designated telephone number beginning with "1900" to receive a recorded announcement or interact with a programme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Second Schedule item 1: this is an audiotex service` MEANS
    `the caller dials a designated telephone number beginning with "1900" to receive a recorded announcement or interact with a programme`

GIVEN `access by users is through the public switched network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all announcements and programmes are pre-recorded and stored in the system, and callers cannot communicate directly in real time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transmission standards of item 4 are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee organised a mass calling event without the Authority's prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the current call charging rate is published in all advertisements and announced at the beginning of the pre-recorded charge announcement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Second Schedule items 2 to 7: the licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `access by users is through the public switched network`
    AND `all announcements and programmes are pre-recorded and stored in the system, and callers cannot communicate directly in real time`
    AND `the transmission standards of item 4 are met`
    AND (NOT `the licensee organised a mass calling event without the Authority's prior approval`)
    AND `the current call charging rate is published in all advertisements and announced at the beginning of the pre-recorded charge announcement`

GIVEN `seconds of the charge announcement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 3 Second Schedule item 8: the first seconds of the call for which the caller is not charged` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `seconds of the charge announcement` LESS THAN 4 THEN JUST 6
           IF `seconds of the charge announcement` AT MOST 10 THEN JUST 12
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `minutes of the call` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Second Schedule item 4(d): the call is within the maximum period without the caller's option to extend` MEANS
    `minutes of the call` AT MOST 10

-- src:TA1999-RG3:278 | 1. The following public switched telecommunication services (whether domestic or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:279 | international) may be resold under this class licence where they are provided through an
-- src:TA1999-RG3:280 | FBO who is licensed to provide public basic telecommunication services, public cellular
-- src:TA1999-RG3:281 | mobile telephone services or public radio paging services:
-- src:TA1999-RG3:282 | (a) public switched telephone services, other than public chain payphone services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:283 | (b) public cellular mobile telephone services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:284 | (c) public radio paging services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:285 | (d) public switched message services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:286 | (e) public switched data services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3:287 | (f) public integrated services digital network services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:288 | (a) an FBO who is licensed to provide public basic telecommunication services,
-- src:TA1999-RG3:289 | public cellular mobile telephone services or public radio paging services; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:290 | (b) an SBO who is licensed to provide international simple resale, mobile virtual
-- src:TA1999-RG3:291 | network operation, international calling card services, internet based voice and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:292 | data services, or call-back and call re-origination services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:294 | Conditions to be complied by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:295 | 2. A licensee must not, except with the approval of the Authority, engage in the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:296 | construction or building of any telecommunication system.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:297 | 3. Where a licensee subscribes to any domestic or international leased circuit, it must
-- src:TA1999-RG3:298 | not, except with the approval of the Authority, provide its users with any direct or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:299 | indirect connection to that leased circuit.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:300 | 4. A licensee must market itself as a reseller of telecommunication services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:301 | 5. A licensee must not charge its users any usage rate higher than the published rates of
-- src:TA1999-RG3:302 | the FBO through which it provides its services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:303 | 6. Notwithstanding paragraph 5, a licensee may charge a maximum set-up charge of 30
-- src:TA1999-RG3:304 | cents for every successful international dialling (IDD) call and 10 cents for every
-- src:TA1999-RG3:305 | successful subscriber trunk dialling (STD) call.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:306 | 7. A licensee must list the rental of equipment charge and the usage charge separately in
-- src:TA1999-RG3:307 | its bills to its users.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:308 | 8. Where a licensee provides the services through resale or shared use of PABX, the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:309 | licensee must not restrict the occupants of the premises served by the PABX from
-- src:TA1999-RG3:310 | subscribing to services or facilities directly from any FBO.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:311 | 9. A licensee must enter into a written service agreement with each of its users.
@ref Rg 3 Third Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:278-311)
GIVEN `service` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Third Schedule item 1: this is a public switched telecommunication service that may be resold under the class licence` MEANS
    elem service (LIST "public switched telephone services, other than public chain payphone services", "public cellular mobile telephone services", "public radio paging services"
                     , "public switched message services", "public switched data services", "public integrated services digital network services")

GIVEN `the licensee constructs or builds a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee provides its users a connection to a leased circuit it subscribes to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee markets itself as a reseller of telecommunication services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the usage rate charged is higher than the published rate of the FBO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee lists the rental of equipment charge and the usage charge separately in its bills` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has a written service agreement with each user` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Third Schedule items 2 to 9: the licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        ((NOT `the licensee constructs or builds a telecommunication system`) OR `the Authority approved it`)
    AND ((NOT `the licensee provides its users a connection to a leased circuit it subscribes to`) OR `the Authority approved it`)
    AND `the licensee markets itself as a reseller of telecommunication services`
    AND (NOT `the usage rate charged is higher than the published rate of the FBO`)
    AND `the licensee lists the rental of equipment charge and the usage charge separately in its bills`
    AND `the licensee has a written service agreement with each user`

GIVEN `call type` IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 3 Third Schedule item 6: the maximum set-up charge in cents for each successful call` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `call type` EQUALS "international dialling (IDD)" THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 10

-- src:TA1999-RG3:319 | 1. Public chain payphone services are the provision of payphone services in multiple
-- src:TA1999-RG3:320 | customer premises through the resale of public switched telephone services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:322 | Conditions to be complied by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:323 | 2. A licensee must not, except with the approval of the Authority, engage in the
-- src:TA1999-RG3:324 | construction or building of any telecommunication system.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:325 | 3. Where a licensee subscribes to any domestic or international leased circuit, it must
-- src:TA1999-RG3:326 | not, except with the approval of the Authority, provide its users with any direct or
-- src:TA1999-RG3:327 | indirect connection to that leased circuit.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:328 | 4. A licensee must market itself as a reseller of telecommunication services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:329 | 5. A licensee must not charge its users any usage rate higher than the published rates of
-- src:TA1999-RG3:330 | the FBO through which it provides its services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:331 | 6. Notwithstanding paragraph 5, the licensee may charge a maximum set-up charge of
-- src:TA1999-RG3:332 | 30 cents for every successful international direct dialling (IDD) call and 10 cents for
-- src:TA1999-RG3:333 | every successful subscriber trunk dialling (STD) call.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:334 | 7. A licensee must comply with the coverage obligations as may, from time to time, be
-- src:TA1999-RG3:335 | set by the Authority for public chain payphone operations.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:336 | 8. A licensee must comply with such quality of service requirements as may, from time
-- src:TA1999-RG3:337 | to time, be determined by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:338 | 9. A licensee must comply with such equal access requirements as may, from time to
-- src:TA1999-RG3:339 | time, be determined by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:340 | 10. A licensee may only resell the services of an FBO and not those of any other
-- src:TA1999-RG3:341 | licensee.
@ref Rg 3 Fourth Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:319-341)
GIVEN `the licensee constructs or builds a telecommunication system, or connects users to a leased circuit, without the Authority's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee markets itself as a reseller of telecommunication services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the usage rate charged is higher than the published rate of the FBO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with the coverage obligations, quality of service requirements and equal access requirements the Authority set` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee resells only the services of an FBO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Fourth Schedule items 2 to 10: the licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        (NOT `the licensee constructs or builds a telecommunication system, or connects users to a leased circuit, without the Authority's approval`)
    AND `the licensee markets itself as a reseller of telecommunication services`
    AND (NOT `the usage rate charged is higher than the published rate of the FBO`)
    AND `the licensee complies with the coverage obligations, quality of service requirements and equal access requirements the Authority set`
    AND `the licensee resells only the services of an FBO`

GIVEN `call type` IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 3 Fourth Schedule item 6: the maximum set-up charge in cents for each successful call` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `call type` EQUALS "international direct dialling (IDD)" THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 10

§ `Rg 3 Fifth to Eighth Schedules`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:350 | 1. Call-back and call re-origination services are International Direct Dial (IDD) call
-- src:TA1999-RG3:351 | reversal services passing over any FBO’s international telephone gateway and public
-- src:TA1999-RG3:352 | switched telecommunication network.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:354 | Conditions to be complied by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:355 | 2. A licensee must not route the voice or data traffic or both over frame-relay or through
-- src:TA1999-RG3:356 | leased circuits.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:357 | 3. A licensee must distinguish its services from IDD services by including the term
-- src:TA1999-RG3:358 | “call-back”, “call re-origination” or its equivalent in its marketing and promotion
-- src:TA1999-RG3:359 | materials.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:360 | 4. A licensee must comply with such minimum Quality of Service (QOS) standards as
-- src:TA1999-RG3:361 | the Authority may, by notice in writing, determine.
@ref Rg 3 Fifth Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:350-361)
GIVEN `the licensee routes voice or data traffic over frame-relay or through leased circuits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee distinguishes its services from IDD services by using the term "call-back", "call re-origination" or its equivalent in its marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with the minimum Quality of Service standards the Authority determined by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Fifth Schedule items 2 to 4: the licensee is meeting the conditions of the call-back and call re-origination class licence` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee routes voice or data traffic over frame-relay or through leased circuits`)
    AND `the licensee distinguishes its services from IDD services by using the term "call-back", "call re-origination" or its equivalent in its marketing`
    AND `the licensee complies with the minimum Quality of Service standards the Authority determined by written notice`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:370 | 1. Internet based voice and data services are the carriage of voice and data services
-- src:TA1999-RG3:371 | through the internet access facilities provided by an SBO.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:372 | Conditions to be complied by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:373 | 2. A licensee must comply with such minimum Quality of Service (QOS) standards as
-- src:TA1999-RG3:374 | the Authority may, by notice in writing, determine.
@ref Rg 3 Sixth Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:370-374)
GIVEN `the licensee complies with the minimum Quality of Service standards the Authority determined by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Sixth Schedule item 2: the licensee is meeting the condition of the internet based voice and data services class licence` MEANS
    `the licensee complies with the minimum Quality of Service standards the Authority determined by written notice`

-- src:TA1999-RG3:383 | 1. The International Calling Card (ICC) services are services that use PIN validation and
-- src:TA1999-RG3:384 | call routing through an FBO’s international telephone gateway to provide IDD services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:386 | Conditions to be complied by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:387 | 2. A licensee must not route voice or data traffic or both over frame-relay or through
-- src:TA1999-RG3:388 | leased circuits.
@ref Rg 3 Seventh Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:383-388)
GIVEN `the licensee routes voice or data traffic over frame-relay or through leased circuits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Seventh Schedule item 2: the licensee is meeting the condition of the international calling card class licence` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee routes voice or data traffic over frame-relay or through leased circuits`)

-- src:TA1999-RG3:397 | 1. Store-and-retrieve value-added network services —
-- src:TA1999-RG3:398 | (a) Where no leased circuits are used No fee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:399 | (b) Where leased circuits are used $200 for 3 years
-- src:TA1999-RG3:402 | 2. Audiotex services $200 for 3 years
-- src:TA1999-RG3:405 | 3. Resale of public switched telecommunication No fee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:406 | services
-- src:TA1999-RG3:409 | 4. Public chain payphone services No fee
-- src:TA1999-RG3:412 | 5. Call-back and call re-origination services $200 for 3 years
-- src:TA1999-RG3:415 | 6. Internet based voice and data services $200 for 3 years
-- src:TA1999-RG3:418 | 7. International calling card service $200 for 3 years.
-- src:TA1999-RG3:420 | PART II — FEES WHERE CLASS LICENCES OVERLAP
-- src:TA1999-RG3:422 | The maximum fee payable by an operator who runs specified telecommunication systems
-- src:TA1999-RG3:423 | and services falling within more than one class licence is $200 for every 3 years.
@ref Rg 3 Eighth Schedule (src:TA1999-RG3:397-423)
GIVEN `type of class licence` IS A STRING
      `leased circuits are used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 3 Eighth Schedule Part I: the registration fee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Store-and-retrieve value-added network services" THEN (IF `leased circuits are used` THEN JUST "$200 for 3 years" ELSE JUST "No fee")
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Audiotex services" THEN JUST "$200 for 3 years"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Resale of public switched telecommunication services" THEN JUST "No fee"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Public chain payphone services" THEN JUST "No fee"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Call-back and call re-origination services" THEN JUST "$200 for 3 years"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Internet based voice and data services" THEN JUST "$200 for 3 years"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "International calling card service" THEN JUST "$200 for 3 years"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `number of overlapping class licences the operator's services fall within` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum of the fees for those licences, in dollars for every 3 years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 3 Eighth Schedule Part II: the fee payable for every 3 years, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `number of overlapping class licences the operator's services fall within` AT MOST 1 THEN `the sum of the fees for those licences, in dollars for every 3 years`
           IF `the sum of the fees for those licences, in dollars for every 3 years` GREATER THAN 200 THEN 200
           OTHERWISE `the sum of the fees for those licences, in dollars for every 3 years`
